<title>FRANCE: Seita being sued for more than 2 mln FFr.</title>
<headline>Seita being sued for more than 2 mln FFr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seita said on Thursday a smoker who has launched a legal suit against the French tobacco company alleging that his cancer was caused by smoking its cigarettes is seeking more than two million francs in damages.</p>
<p>The figure was given by a Seita spokeswoman.</p>
<p>She added the company was &quot;absolutely confident&quot; about the outcome of the case, which is the first of its kind brought in France.</p>
<p>&quot;No money has ever been paid out anywhere&quot; for such proceedings, she said, citing especially cases in the United States.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
